      "created_at": "2019-01-14T01:15:17Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-01-14T01:15:17Z",
      "body": "Why can't you? Why would you default to unable to set cookies?  Secure should only be used if certs are specified in the configuration for that connection i.e. { tls: { cert:\"\", key:\"\" }}.  Setting secure for any other reason will make cookies completely useless.  If most node production deployment use HTTP then I would think you wouldn't want secure set, as there is no browser that would even accept those cookies, ever.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
