      "created_at": "2019-01-14T01:24:32Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-01-14T01:26:06Z",
      "body": "The trick is that deployments often do use HTTPS, but terminate TLS _in front_ of the node server, i.e. at a reverse proxy or load balancer, and there's no way for hapi to know if that is going to be the case.  Notice how in this case secure cookies are still fully able to be used with hapi, even if the hapi server itself does not use TLS.",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
