      "created_at": "2019-01-14T09:02:59Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-01-14T09:02:59Z",
      "body": "No I understand that, but then wouldn't the configurer TURN ON SECURE manually because they are going use it?  What i'm not understanding, i guess. Is why is the default to be in a broken state where cookies cannot be used. Non TLS/SSL should default to non secure, TLS/SSL should default to secure, with the ability to override that if needed.  I'm just saying the DEFAULT should take into account the state of the connection, instead of always saying true or false.",
